From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 02:58:01 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: scaler: add the mem2mem device for same-size
 conversion

Expose the engine as a V4L2 memory-to-memory device. The OUTPUT queue
takes NV12, NV12M, P010, ARGB32 or XRGB32, the CAPTURE queue any of
them at the same size. Y'CbCr to R'G'B' and back uses the colorimetry of
the Y'CbCr side (BT.601, BT.709 or BT.2020, limited or full range); the
R'G'B' side is full range and keeps the primaries and transfer function,
since the engine only changes the encoding.

Each job is written with MMIO in one go from the register list the job
builder produces, START last. Completion and errors arrive on the MSR
interrupt; an error or a 500 ms timeout fails the job and resets the
engine through its power-domain reset before the next one. Interrupts
are enabled on the first job after every power-up.

Not yet tested on hardware: the DT nodes stay disabled until the
qualification run.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit 9b03f5b433ee9bc819a8dbe2aa136fe4cde80245)
